  "complexity": 6,
  "title": "S3a evidence reuse from cancelled or failed workers: partial results become evidence objects with provenance worker_partial, routed to the replacement worker (P27)",
  "spec": "orchestrator/evidence.py: add provenance value worker_partial to PROVENANCE (trust_class LOCAL_USER, trust field untrusted stays as for non-repo provenance, scan applied as for any evidence). orchestrator/worker_control.py: after cancel builds the partial result, and in a new hook worker_control.preserve_partial(task) that daemon.reconcile_dead calls for a dead worker with a dirty worktree, create evidence objects in the goal's evidence pool (evidence.make with source_type worker_partial, location the task id plus the worktree head sha, content = the partial facts rendered as compact lines: files changed with diff stat, commits with subjects, tests run and their result lines, error tail, files inspected; commit = worktree head sha; freshness by the existing hash mechanism). Replacement routing: orchestrator/context_router.py treats worker_partial evidence whose location task shares the same goal and overlaps the current task's scope (write or read) as high relevance (never HIDE) with a cap of [context_router].partial_max_tokens (default 800, dated comment); orchestrator/spawn.py renders those items under a packet section prior_worker (after evidence) with the source task id and the head sha, so the new worker can check out or diff it instead of rediscovering; the section is empty when nothing applies. Docs: docs/hermes-hardening/16-evidence-reuse.md.\nSpec review T-1198 folded in: (1) evidence.py: add worker_partial to BOTH SOURCE_TYPES and PROVENANCE (make() validates each separately) and add an explicit entry worker_partial -> LOCAL_USER in the _trust_class dict, documenting in the module docstring that LOCAL_USER covers locally produced artifacts (memory and observed worker outputs), not only user-authored memory. (2) fresh() and context_router's duplicate/staleness check are extended so worker_partial evidence goes stale when its commit differs from the goal head (same commit == head_sha rule as source_chunk and test_result). (3) Shadow-first: the prior_worker section is rendered only when [context_router].mode is active; in shadow the would-be section (ids and chars) is logged on the context_route decision row and the packet is unchanged. (4) preserve_partial is idempotent: it stamps pipeline.partial_preserved_at on the task and returns early when the stamp exists, so reconcile_dead re-runs every tick without growing the pool. (5) Overlap is computed from persisted data only: the dead task's write scope against the current task's write scope plus its packet-time read scope; no read footprint of the dead task is stored. (6) tests/test_worker_control.py exists with class WorkerControl; add the new test as a method there.\nSpec review T-1211 folded in: (1) The evidence object gains an optional field scope (list of paths, default empty, persisted and backfilled like trust_class); preserve_partial fills it with the dead task's write scope, so context_router.relevance_for computes worker_partial overlap from ev.scope against the current task's write scope plus packet-time read scope; the location stays task_id:head_sha and bus.py is untouched. (2) Precedence: staleness wins; a worker_partial item whose commit is not the goal head is HIDE (stale), and only a fresh overlapping item is 'never HIDE'. (3) The cap is enforced at creation time: preserve_partial truncates the rendered content to [context_router].partial_max_tokens times 4 chars (mirroring worker_control._bounded_result), so the router needs no per-item cap. (4) SOURCE_TYPES, PROVENANCE and the _trust_class entry change together in one commit with one test that make(source_type=worker_partial, provenance=worker_partial) succeeds and yields LOCAL_USER.\nRepository rules: unittest (not pytest), tests/_harness.py single ORCH_ROOT fixture; every acceptance test id tests/test_<module>.py::test_name is a method def test_name(self) in a unittest.TestCase. No new third-party dependencies. Never write secret values to any file or log; test fixtures use synthetic names and values that are not credential-shaped. Do not quote template placeholder tokens (double braces) anywhere in code comments or docs. Shadow-first: a new adaptive path never changes what a worker sees until its mode is active; shadow only writes decision_log or runs rows. Task worktrees carry no .orchestrator runs, tasks or decision_log state: tests use synthetic fixtures; for any measured numbers in docs run read-only against /Users/k3ntaw/code/orchestrator/.orchestrator via an explicit root argument. Run .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh . until green; the base suite must stay green. Do not ask questions: decide, and note decisions in the result summary. Contracts of the earlier modules: .orchestrator/plan.md (section GOAL T-0991) and docs/hermes-hardening/*.md on this branch; read the merged modules before building on them.",
